> (which is generally pronounced /&#716;w&#618;k&#618;'pi:di&#601;/ or
> /&#716;wiki'pi:di&#601;/ in English). There doesn't seem to be a consensus
> there (and not a very active discussion, really), so I thought I'd solicit
> some opinions from the list. The options seem to be {uikipedias}, which is
> what appears in the logo, or {uikiPEdi,as}, which is how it's written on
> the front page. I think I prefer the former (which I read
> /wi.ki.'p&#603;d.j&#593;s/ -- I hope that's correct); the CLL implies that
> it's better to have emphasis on the penultimate syllable, and I think this
> achieves a more Lojbanic sound.
>
> I feel like this worth getting straight because it's embarrassing to
> Lojbanic project that can't even spell the name of the project
> consistently.
>
> I, to boot, don't really see any particular reason why the Lojban word for
